<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gyeongae of Silla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 927</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as King Gyeongae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gyeongae was king of Silla from 924 to 927, during the Later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-kingdoms-period">Three Kingdoms period</a>, when Silla had shrunk to a small state around its capital. In 927 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeon-hwon">Gyeon Hwon</a> of Later Baekje sacked the capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeongju">Gyeongju</a> and forced the king to take his own life, placing Gyeongsun on the throne. The outrage turned Silla towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taejo-of-goryeo">Wang Geon</a> of Goryeo, to whom it later surrendered.</p></div>
